td-term native conformance corpus
=================================

This is td-term's normative behavioral corpus. Imported and td-authored cases
use the same line-oriented format and live together by subject. Every case has
a stable id, a source, feature tags, an initial size, at least one operation,
and at least one observable expectation.

Operations are `write`, `resize`, and `key`. A `key` chord is `[modifier+...]name`
over the adapter's own key table, where a modifier is `ctrl`, `alt`, `shift`,
`caps`, or `super` -- the last so a case can pin that a compositor chord the
terminal does not translate reaches the child as nothing at all -- and a name
is that table's spelling of an evdev code (`a`, `f12`,
`pageup`, `kp7`). Each press runs through the keyboard adapter with the modes
the terminal is in at that point, so an application-cursor case establishes the
mode with a `write` and then observes the answer.

`expect input` names the adapter's complete generated byte stream since case
initialization, which is separate from `expect reply`: keys generate one, the
terminal generates the other, and the PTY writer merges them only later. A key
this profile deliberately does not translate contributes no bytes rather than
being a corpus error.

`expect viewport` names how many lines back the scrollback viewport sits,
which no byte stream reports: a key routed to the viewport reaches neither
the child nor the terminal, so its whole effect is that number. What the
viewport SHOWS is the renderer's, and the render spec is where it is
checked -- these cases pin which key moves it, and how far.

libvterm-0.3.3.term is generated from the pinned MIT-licensed v0.3.3 archive.
Its report accounts for every source case and assertion; LICENSE.libvterm
retains the upstream license. The archive and legacy Perl/C harness are not
build inputs.

The std-only importer verifies every source-file hash before generating output:

  cargo run --manifest-path td-compositor/Cargo.toml \
    --bin td-term-import-libvterm -- check LIBVTERM-0.3.3 \
    td-compositor/spec/term

Run the ignored `print_semantic_expectations_overlay` test to regenerate the
exact xfail set. Unexpected failures, passes, stale entries, unknown tags, and
malformed input all red the gate.
